<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Rails on Pablo Fonseca</title><link>https://pablobfonseca.github.io/categories/rails/</link><description>Recent content in Rails on Pablo Fonseca</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 22 Aug 2016 18:00:00 -0300</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://pablobfonseca.github.io/categories/rails/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Make non ActiveRecord classes renderable</title><link>https://pablobfonseca.github.io/posts/make-non-activerecord-renderable/</link><pubDate>Mon, 22 Aug 2016 18:00:00 -0300</pubDate><guid>https://pablobfonseca.github.io/posts/make-non-activerecord-renderable/</guid><description>&lt;p>In order to render a new partial without being a &amp;ldquo;Rails&amp;rdquo; object we can rewrite the method &lt;code>to_partial_path&lt;/code> to do so:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div class="chroma">
&lt;table class="lntable">&lt;tr>&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code>&lt;span class="lnt">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">2
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">3
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">4
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">5
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">class&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Timeline&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nf">to_partial_path&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;timeline/timeline&amp;#34;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">end&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">end&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>Now we just need to create the view in &lt;code>app/views/timeline/_timeline.htm.erb&lt;/code> and it&amp;rsquo;s going to work like a charm!&lt;/p>
&lt;p>or, we can extend the &lt;code>ActiveModel::Naming&lt;/code> to make it works as well:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div class="chroma">
&lt;table class="lntable">&lt;tr>&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code>&lt;span class="lnt">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">2
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">3
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">class&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Timeline&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="kp">extend&lt;/span> &lt;span class="no">ActiveModel&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">::&lt;/span>&lt;span class="no">Naming&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">end&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;q>Happy coding!&lt;/q>&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>